   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Dear all,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">I have a large phylogeny (625 species). The pdfs produced when I run the analyses and not useful for me since everything is clogged in one page so I&#39;d like to hand pick my nodes of interest (and their range_probabilities) to manually add pie charts (i.e) in these nodes by other means.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">In the <b>trtable</b> I can see the daughters nodes for each node. However when I plot the the nodes</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><b>plot(tr, label.offset=0.3, tipcex=0.3, statecex=0.3,cex = 0.3)</b></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><b>axisPhylo()</b></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><b>nodelabels()</b></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">it&#39;s difficult to hand pick the nodes of interest. </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/biogeobears/attach/70d1c026a75b/Rplot_nodes.jpeg?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" width=\"348\" height=\"385\" style=\"margin-right:0px\"><br>​<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Is there a way of exporting the tree with the nodes numbers on it, so I can make sure I&#39;m choosing the right nodes? Or any other solution?<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Any idea is welcome.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Best for ow,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Boni</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">​​</div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Esther Nieto<div>PhD Student</div><div>Department of Biology</div><div>Memorial University of Newfoundland</div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">St. John&#39;s, NL, </span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">A1B 3X9, Canada</span><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://julissaroncal.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://julissaroncal.wordpress.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485272396000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1bAtvXfxueshy_tocRuJZ7\">https://julissaroncal.wordpress.com/</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://antonelli-lab.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://antonelli-lab.net/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485272396000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iL06Q0ejWKvqYqthRoT5g\">http://antonelli-lab.net/</a><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n"
