   "subject": "Re: [BioGeoBEARS] Targeting specific nodes for range_probabilities",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi! Thanks for using the group.<div><br></div><div>Your best option to see all of the node numbers is to plot the tree into a PDF with a large height.</div><div><br></div><div>So, something like:</div><div><br></div><div>=================================</div><div># Open PDF for writing</div><div><div>pdffn = &quot;whatever_name.pdf&quot;</div><div># Height is 30 inches</div><div>pdf(file=pdffn, width=8, height=30)</div></div><div><br></div><div>[put plotting tr + node numbers code here]</div><div><br></div><div><div># Close PDF writing</div><div></div></div><div><div>dev.off()</div><div><br></div><div># Open PDF viewing</div><div>cmdstr = paste0(&quot;open &quot;, pdffn)</div><div>system(cmdstr)</div></div><div>=================================</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Nick</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Jan 11, 2016 at 4:14 AM, Nieto Blazquez, Maria Esther <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">men...@mun.ca</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
